.TH FREE 1 "November 2026" "free 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
free \- display the amount of free and used memory (macOS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B free
shows the total, used and free physical memory and swap space, in the same
format as the Linux procps-ng \fBfree\fR(1) command.
Values are read from Mach VM statistics (\fBhost_statistics64\fR) and from
\fBsysctl\fR (\fBhw.memsize\fR, \fBvm.swapusage\fR).
.SS Columns
.TP
.B total
Physical memory (\fBhw.memsize\fR).
.TP
.B used
total \- free \- buff/cache (the Linux formula).
.TP
.B free
Free pages, excluding speculative pages (\fBvm_stat\fR "Pages free").
.TP
.B shared
No macOS equivalent; always 0.
.TP
.B buff/cache
File-backed and purgeable pages.
.TP
.B available
total \- (app memory + wired + compressed); the complement of Activity
Monitor's "Memory Used".
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bytes
Display in bytes.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kibi
Display in kibibytes (default).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mebi
Display in mebibytes.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gibi
Display in gibibytes.
.TP
.BR \-\-tebi ", " \-\-pebi
Display in tebibytes / pebibytes.
.TP
.BR \-\-kilo ", " \-\-mega ", " \-\-giga ", " \-\-tera ", " \-\-peta
Display in powers of 1000.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-human
Human-readable output (B, Ki, Mi, Gi...).
.TP
.B \-\-si
Use powers of 1000 instead of 1024.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wide
Show buffers and cache in separate columns. macOS uses a unified buffer
cache, so buffers is always 0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-total
Add a line with RAM + swap totals.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-line
One-line summary.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-detail
macOS-specific breakdown: app, wired, compressed, file-backed, purgeable,
speculative.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seconds " \fIN\fR"
Refresh every \fIN\fR seconds (fractions allowed).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " \fIN\fR"
Refresh \fIN\fR times, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH NOTES
\fB\-l\fR/\fB\-\-lohi\fR and \fB\-v\fR/\fB\-\-committed\fR are Linux-specific
and are not supported on macOS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vm_stat (1),
.BR sysctl (8),
.BR memory_pressure (1)
